          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l12",
          "reminder": "Replacing x by |x| reflects the right-hand graph into the left half-plane."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Make the area positive",
      "body": "<p>Decide whether the enclosed region is above or below the x-axis. Write an integral for the gap between the curve and the axis on the positive side.</p>",
      "recap": "Area between two curves is the integral of upper height minus lower height.",
      "pitfall": "Geometric area cannot be negative.",
      "pause": "Find the limits and choose the correct order for the subtraction.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Area between two curves is the integral of upper height minus lower height."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Use the symmetry after integrating",
      "body": "<p>Integrate the polynomial gap and evaluate it at your limits. Use the symmetry of the graph to obtain the whole enclosed area.</p>",
      "recap": "Integrate each power, then subtract the antiderivative values at the two limits.",
      "pitfall": "Keep track of which half of the region your integral covers.",
      "pause": "Finish the integration and calculate the total area.",
      "recall": [
